  <iati-identifier>US-GOV-1-649-22-IO(FAO)-003</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="US-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Agency for International Development</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RECOVER - Reducing Communities&#x2019; Vulnerability to Drought and External Shocks (FAO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Somalia):  With FY 2024 funds, USAID will strengthen leadership and governance structures by establishing committees to address production, performing infrastructure maintenance, undertaking disaster risk mitigation, and building financial literacy capacity. Additionally, Reducing Communities&apos; Vulnerability to Drought and External Shocks (RECOVER) will build capacity in post-harvest techniques such as grain-quality management, improve access to post-harvest equipment such as moisture meters, and invest in grain and cereal storage infrastructure. To improve marketing opportunities, RECOVER will enhance the ability of farmers to aggregate their grain and produce by connecting them with traders while exploring value-addition opportunities. Further, RECOVER will strengthen group governance among cooperatives to increase access to finance through Multinational Finance Institutions..RECOVER is carefully designed to address the interlinked challenges arising from areas prone to climatic hazards and vulnerabilities as well as endemic conflict due to competing land claims, geographical segregation, and moribund local economies, which encourage predation and rent-seeking. In addition to the large-scale infrastructure rehabilitation, the program involves activities that address conflict mitigation, stabilization, and peacebuilding; control flood and soil erosion; strengthen climate-smart production techniques; and increase capacity for effective governance. RECOVER also includes a crisis response mechanism to enable a rapid response when gains achieved by the activity are threatened....</narrative>
  </description>
